<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Merrymakers on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/merrymakers/</link><description>Recent content in Merrymakers on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 21 May 2013 09:01:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/merrymakers/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>What is the font?</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/103200/</link><pubDate>Tue, 21 May 2013 09:01:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/103200/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This logo was designed for us by an advertising agency designer who has since left the agency. The CD has no record of the work, and I have had no luck trying to identify the font. One special feature of the font is the letter &amp;ldquo;k&amp;rdquo;. Does anyone know the name of this font?&lt;/p&gt;
